1. The Core Problem & Financial Opportunity
Sidewalk delivery and autonomous mobile robot (AMR) fleets face a strict unit-economics ceiling driven by asset underutilization:

The Idle Window: Delivery AMRs sit idle from 11:00 PM to 6:00 AM, generating zero revenue while fixed hardware depreciation and cloud connectivity costs accumulate.

The Revenue Vector: Automated driveway-to-curb waste management generates $20–$30/month per home.

Fleet Yield: A 500-home suburban cluster yields $120,000–$180,000 in high-margin Annual Recurring Revenue (ARR) using existing fleet assets overnight.
2. Engineering Bottlenecks vs. The "Hub & Spoke" Solution
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        THE HUB & SPOKE PARADIGM                        │
├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ THE SPOKES (Lightweight AMRs)    ►   THE HUB (Stationary Mechanics)    │
│ • Low-cost, low-mass tugs            • Grid-powered heavy hydraulics  │
│ • Focus 100% on TRANSIT               • Focuses 100% on DUMPING        │
│ • ANSI Z245 standard rim/pin clamp    • Does the 400-lb heavy lifting  │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
Legacy Flaw: Mounting hydraulic dumpers on mobile chassis spikes vehicle mass, ruins battery endurance, inflates BOM, and creates severe safety/OSHA liability.

OWRA Solution: Decouple horizontal transit from vertical dumping.
Spoke (AMR): Light, low-cost tug equipped with standard ANSI Z245 clamps.
Hub (Dock/Truck): Wall-mounted dock tippers (commercial) or municipal side-loader trucks (residential) handle all vertical dumping

3. Strategic ROI & Execution
Modular Platform Synergy: A single standardized core chassis powers both commercial and residential payloads, delivering a 50% R&D time reduction and a 40% lower unit manufacturing cost.
Immediate Deployment: Firm-level integration requires zero cart customization; vehicles target existing, ubiquitous ANSI 64/96-gallon rolling bins.
Execution Ready: Parametric OpenSCAD CAD models, ROS 2 nodes, and deterministic 100Hz RTOS C state machine drivers are open-sourced and ready for platform validation
